meta {
  name: Send ash online link email
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/send-links/ashonline
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "name": "John Doe"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

docs {
  # Send ASH Online Link Email
  
  Sends the ASH Online registration link to a recipient via email. The service renders an EJS email template (`ash-online-registration-link.ejs`) and dispatches the email using Brevo.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `POST /api/v1/send-links/ashonline`
  
  ## Request Body
  The request expects a JSON object with the following fields:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Constraints | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `email` | string | Yes | Must be a valid email address | The recipient's email address. |
  | `name` | string | Yes | Min: 3 characters, Max: 256 characters | The recipient's name (used in the email template). |
  
  ## Success Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - **Body**:
    ```json
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "ASH ONLINE Registration email sent successfully",
      "data": null,
      "meta": {
        "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
      }
    }
    ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation failed (e.g., invalid email, name too short).
  - **429 Too Many Requests**: Rate limit exceeded (`sendLinksLimiter`: 5 requests per 15-minute window, keyed by IP).
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: 
    - Failed to render the EJS email template.
    - Brevo API error (email transporter failure).
    - Email delivery verification failed — thrown when `sendEmail` returns a falsy value (e.g., `"ASH ONLINE Registration Email was not sent"`).
  
  ## Rate Limiting
  This endpoint is protected by `sendLinksLimiter` — a maximum of **5 requests per 15-minute window**, keyed by the client's IP address. Exceeds return a `429` with `{ code: "RATE_LIMITED", message: "Too many request attempts. Please try again later" }`.
  
  ## Notes
  - The generated link points to `/social-initiatives/ash-online/register` based on `FRONTEND_BASEURL`.
  - No caching is involved — this endpoint triggers a transactional email on every call.
}
